Carried patch, Windows only: LIBXSMM's POWER generator under LLP64.

LIBXSMM 2.1.0's ppc64le generator keeps 64-bit prefixed instruction words in
unsigned long, which is 32 bits on Windows. -Werror=overflow fails
generator_gemm_mma_microkernel.c, and generator_ppc64le_instructions.c switches
on a 64-bit form index whose case labels all truncate to 0, a duplicate case
error. The code never runs on x86; it is still compiled. The type is the same
width on LP64, so nothing changes there. Still present in 2.1.0, the tag Palace
0.19.0 pins.

